Latest ascension below.  Didn't go for any conducts this time round as
I was getting a bit jaded and wanted to just have some fun.  Next I'm
going to try and foodless weaponless Monk for a bit of variety.

Started with cure sickness and detect monsters.  There were two altars
on the first level, neutral and chaotic.  Sacrificed at the neutral one
and eventually got Magicbane.

Found speed boots in a general store on dlvl 5.  Raided the rest of the
general store for various items.

Found Piper's grave on dlvl 7.  Lots of spellbooks, a magic lamp, two
wands of poly and a magic marker - clearly Piper had been a wizard.
These would have to wait until later, since Dizzy's Int was only 9.
Set up camp at the altar on dlvl 6 to sort through the stuff and store
spare gear.

The Oracle level had no Oracle - I only had a pet cat and a horse, so I
assume they didn't kill it...

Did Soko and got the amulet.  Back to the stash to sort out some stuff,
and then back to Soko to reverse gen nurses.  HP went from 89 to 165.
Went back to the stash and used the magic lamp to wish for a blessed
fixed +2 helm of brilliance, raising my Int to 12.  That turned out to
be enough to read the spellbooks I had accumulated so far.
Unfortunately no identify yet.

Decided to head down the mines.  Found a very expensive spellbook in a
shop - hopefully the finger but would need to find out when I was a
little more intelligent.  Found a spare bag of holding on the way down.

Near the bottom of the mines found the grave of jon who had been killed
by a stone giant.  His grave provided +2 gdsm, spare speed boots and a
load of wands.

Got the luckstone and headed back to the main stash to do some more
sacrificing - was looking for a spellbook of identify or mjollnir.  Got
trollsbane, but no luck. Kept sacrificing but no mojo - got crowned
instead.  Gave up and decided to descend.

Found gauntlets of power on the way down.

Found a poly trap on dlvl 14.  Also picked up a figurine of an
elvenking on the level.  Transformed the cat into a balrog and the
elvenking into an Aleax.  Went back to kill all the shopkeepers and
donated the gold to get naked AC 1.

Went back up to the stash to use a wand of poly on the pile of
spellbooks in an attempt to get identify and create monster.  Got
indentify.  Used up both wands of poly on piles of useless rings
(having collected them from sinks) but failed to get slow digestion.
Got free action though.

Decided to go and do the quest instead.  Turned out to be pretty easy -
my pets killed the nemesis before I'd really noticed him.  Went back to
the stash to sort through some stuff and try to get a decent weapon,
but only ended up getting Giantslayer.  Decided to proceed with
Trollsbane for the time being.

Descended again.  Found Ludios on dlvl 19.  Cleared it, donated all the
gold, got pets to kill the priest at the temple on dlvl 10, took all
the gold to minetown to donate, got pets the kill the priest.  Sacc'd
until I got Mojo (took a very long time - priests should not be given
edged weapons as sacrifice gifts as this is illogical).  Around turn
51,300 got Mojo.  Back at the stash, poly'd a pile of unihorns and got
3 magic markers (94, 63, 31 charges).  Enchanted Mojo up to +6 and most
armour to +4 to take AC to -34.  Poly'd some rings and finally got slow
digestion.  Convinced the Aleax to pick up Werebane.  Then decided to
descend to Medusa and the castle.

On the way down donated all my gold to the last remaining priest, and
lowered naked AC to -4.

Killed Medusa; Perseus had the boots and the shield.  Enchanted and
wore the shield (although it greatly increased failure rates) and
increased AC to -42.

The castle wand was 0:2.

Got all coins from previous priest and then donated them to VotD
priest. to get naked AC -5.  Wished up a t-shirt and enchanted it to +4
to get AC down to -53.

Mapped Gehennom with magic mapping and dug tunnels - first time I
haven't explored the levels.  Got to the bottom, marked the VS, did
almost all of Rodney's tower and then went back up to the stash to sort
through my stuff.  Alchemy boosted max HP from 211 to 459.  Decided to
improve spellcasting by ditching shield of reflection, so AC went up to
-46.

Paused for several months because the final ascension run is a bit
boring.

Picked up the appropriate gear from the stash for the run, went down,
killed Rodney, infiltrated the Sanctum.  Got up to Jubilex to discover
my ring of lev had disappeared, so wished up a new one.

Rodney didn't appear very often; the planes weren't really a problem.

